From 6d34d48562b7299c5d8b3c0605272669657e9b67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:37:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Gate remote notice and outcome passes on semantic
 inputs

Replica task liveness writes were invalidating both settled notice and card-change proofs every host pass. Retain quiet notice inputs across irrelevant row deltas and distinguish stale seeded observations from deliverable late notices. Use per-task content cursors plus status/owner/chat-link fingerprints for outcome fanout, not rebuilt ledger object identities.

Proof: real-cursor heartbeat/rebuilt-ledger regression fails on parent da4e09cf72 (5 reads versus 2), passes after the change. Status, owner, link, deletion, missing-row and raced-projection controls pass. Removing the post-projection cursor fence fails the race control. Host-gate tests cover first-seen terminal/withdrawal states, replica restore identity, concurrent writes and backward clocks. Required CI, independent exact-head review, and deployed 600-second CPU acceptance remain mandatory.
